00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.909
Quick note I don't want to spend a ton of
time on this, but Donald Trump has decided

00:06:14.909 --> 00:06:16.800
to cancel the event that he had planned for
tomorrow.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.900
Trump was going to do a press conference at
Mar a Lago, his Florida resort, tomorrow,

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.479
January six, 2022, the one year anniversary
of the Trump riots on January six, 2021.

00:06:21.479 --> 00:06:22.479
He has now canceled that.

00:06:22.479 --> 00:06:23.479
Maggie Haberman from the New York Times says
that quote, among other things, several advisers,

00:06:23.479 --> 00:06:24.479
former formal and informal, told Trump the
press conference was a mistake, and it was

00:06:24.479 --> 00:06:25.479
becoming clear he wasn't likely to get the
live TV coverage that he was hoping for.

00:06:25.479 --> 00:06:26.479
So there's actually two interpretations of
Trump's decision to cancel this.

00:06:26.479 --> 00:06:27.479
One is he realized there's no way to spin
what happened last January 6th in any way,

00:06:27.479 --> 00:06:28.479
in any way that would be remotely advantageous
to him.

00:06:28.479 --> 00:06:29.479
That's one possibility.

00:06:29.479 --> 00:06:32.020
Trump's ego tends to push in the other direction,
which is I can always spin anything to be

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:33.020
good for me.

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:36.000
So the other interpretation is Trump got word
that the major networks were not going to

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.100
be carrying that press conference live and
decided it wasn't going to get the publicity

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.100
that he wanted.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.100
And that really does anger the guy.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.100
So that has been canceled.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.100
Important.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:43.100
Donald Trump will be appearing at a rally
in the state of Arizona, not this Saturday,

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.100
